  #line-at(475.18pt, 473.95pt, "3.2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(488.98pt, 473.95pt, ". By contrast, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 489.55pt, "the spin-coated PI film exhibits markedly weaker thermal anisotropy, with an anisotropy ratio of approximately ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(521.74pt, 489.55pt, "1.6 −")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 505.15pt, "1.7")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(63.384pt, 505.15pt, ", while its cross-plane thermal conductivity increases to ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.63pt, 505.15pt, "0.29 −0.34 W/(m ⋅K)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(405.19pt, 505.15pt, ". These results indicate that film-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 520.75pt, "processing routes can substantially alter chain orientation and through-thickness packing in PI films and thereby change ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 536.35pt, "both in-plane and cross-plane heat conduction. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 551.95pt, "Polarized Raman spectroscopy further supports this interpretation. The spin-coated PI film shows a higher ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 567.55pt, "depolarization ratio than the commercial film, indicating a more nearly isotropic molecular orientation; this is consistent ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 583.18pt, "with its lower thermal-conductivity anisotropy and higher measured cross-plane thermal conductivity. Importantly, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 598.78pt, "volumetric heat capacity need not equal a bulk or literature value and can depend on film density, curing history, and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 614.38pt, "molecular packing. Direct measurement of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(235.49pt, 614.38pt, "𝐶")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(242.21pt, 614.38pt, " in such process-sensitive films therefore helps reduce systematic error ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 629.98pt, "introduced by an assumed heat-capacity input. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 646.3pt, "It should also be noted that simultaneous decoupling of ")
