  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 7.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(345.43pt, 671.14pt, "𝑧")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(349.87pt, 668.98pt, ". In low-symmetry crystals, off-cut crystals, or ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 684.58pt, "materials whose crystallographic axes are not aligned with the device coordinate system, however, heat flux and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 700.18pt, "temperature gradient need not be parallel, and the thermal-conductivity tensor in the experimental coordinate system ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 715.78pt, "can contain off-diagonal components. In such cases, a thermoreflectance signal no longer reflects an effective ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 731.38pt, "conductivity along a single direction, but is jointly determined by multiple tensor components, making reconstruction ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 747pt, "of the full three-dimensional conductivity tensor a substantially more challenging measurement problem. ")
