  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(280.25pt, 115.1pt, " in films or crystals. Elliptical-beam TDTR [75], beam-offset ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 130.7pt, "TDTR [67], and beam-offset FDTR [69] further introduce lateral spatial resolution so that differences in heat diffusion ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 146.3pt, "along different in-plane directions can be detected. SDTR directly scans the spatial distribution of the surface thermal ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 161.9pt, "response and provides an especially intuitive physical picture for measuring in-plane thermal diffusivity and in-plane ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 177.5pt, "anisotropy [39]. Together, these developments have expanded thermoreflectance from early measurements dominated ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 193.1pt, "by cross-plane transport to quantitative analysis of directional heat transport with angular resolution. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 208.7pt, "Even so, measuring only effective in-plane and normal-direction conductivities is insufficient to reconstruct a ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 224.3pt, "complete three-dimensional conductivity tensor. In particular, when the crystallographic principal axes are not aligned ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 239.9pt, "with the sample-surface coordinate system, the thermal-conductivity tensor in the experimental coordinates can be ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 255.53pt, "written as ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(248.69pt, 286.73pt, "𝐤= [")
  #line-at(273.17pt, 271.37pt, "𝑘")
