  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.584pt, 317.93pt, "Both diagonal and off-diagonal terms can influence the surface temperature field. The contributions of different ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 333.53pt, "tensor components to the thermoreflectance signal vary with modulation frequency, beam-offset direction, and probe ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 349.13pt, "position, and the components can be strongly coupled. A single modulation frequency, one spatial scan direction, or a ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 364.73pt, "fit that prescribes part of the tensor is therefore generally insufficient for stable reconstruction of the complete tensor. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 380.33pt, "Three-dimensional tensor estimation requires enough independent frequency, spatial, and directional constraints, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 395.93pt, "together with sensitivity analysis to determine whether the individual components are separable. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 411.55pt, "AT-cut quartz provides a representative example. Its crystallographic c axis (the optical or Z axis of quartz) is ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 427.15pt, "inclined relative to the sample surface, with an angle of approximately ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(348.19pt, 427.15pt, "35.25°")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.59pt, 427.15pt, " between the cut plane and the c axis. In ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 442.75pt, "the experimental coordinate system, the conductivity tensor contains not only the principal in-plane components (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(527.86pt, 442.75pt, "𝑘")
