#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "DengXian", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.85pt, 803.64pt, "32 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 68.28pt, "relative responses of the tensor components. BO-SPS provides one implementation in this particular case; the same ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 83.9pt, "methodological principle can also be explored on other thermoreflectance platforms capable of multidirectional spatial ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 99.5pt, "scanning and multi-condition control. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 130.82pt, "4.4 Multilayer Heterostructures: Selective Estimation of Combined Parameters ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.584pt, 154.1pt, "In wide-bandgap semiconductor devices and heterogeneous integration structures, heat transport commonly ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 169.7pt, "involves multiple functional films, buffer layers, buried interfaces, and supporting substrates. In representative power-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 185.3pt, "device structures such as GaN/Si, GaN/SiC, and GaN/diamond, heat generated during operation must be dissipated ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 200.9pt, "sequentially through metal contacts, the GaN epitaxial layer, transition or buffer layers, semiconductor/substrate ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 216.5pt, "interfaces, and a high-thermal-conductivity substrate [55]. The thermoreflectance signal is therefore influenced ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 232.1pt, "simultaneously by film thermal conductivity, volumetric heat capacity, interfacial thermal conductance, layer thickness, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 247.73pt, "metal-transducer parameters, and substrate properties. If the in-plane conductivity, cross-plane conductivity, volumetric ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 263.33pt, "heat capacity, interfacial thermal conductance, and thickness of every layer are all treated as independent fitting ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 278.93pt, "parameters, the number of unknowns grows rapidly and the inverse problem becomes highly ill-posed. The key to ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 294.53pt, "multilayer-heterostructure measurement is therefore not simply to increase the number of fitting parameters, but to ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 310.13pt, "identify the combinations of parameters to which the signal is genuinely sensitive and determine whether those ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 325.73pt, "combinations can be separated using different frequencies, heat-diffusion scales, or portions of the waveform. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 341.33pt, "TDTR and FDTR have developed a substantial application base for thermophysical characterization of wide-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 356.93pt, "bandgap semiconductor heterostructures. For epitaxial GaN/SiC, Cho et al. used TDTR to study samples with different ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 372.53pt, "GaN thicknesses and obtained the GaN film thermal conductivity and GaN-SiC interfacial thermal conductance, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 388.13pt, "providing important experimental information for thermal-resistance analysis in HEMT devices [81]. TDTR was ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 403.73pt, "subsequently applied to bonded GaN/SiC, GaN/SiC with AlN transition layers, and epitaxial GaN/SiC, GaN/AlN, and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 419.35pt, "AlN/SiC wafers to examine how epitaxial quality, transition layers, and interface structure affect interfacial thermal ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 434.95pt, "conductance [82-84]. For integration with high-thermal-conductivity substrates, Cheng et al. used TDTR to measure ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 450.55pt, "the thermal conductance of bonded GaN/diamond interfaces and combined the thermal measurements with structural ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 466.15pt, "analysis to show how bonding-layer thickness and interface quality affect heat dissipation [85]. TDTR has also been ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 481.75pt, "used for ultrawide-bandgap heterogeneously integrated systems such as β-Ga₂O₃/SiC to measure film thermal ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 497.35pt, "conductivity and buried-interface thermal conductance, and a dual-modulation-frequency TDTR imaging method has ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 512.95pt, "been developed to visualize spatial variations in the buried interfacial thermal conductance of β-Ga₂O₃/SiC [86]. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 528.55pt, "FDTR continuously scans modulation frequency to vary thermal penetration depth, causing the relative ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 544.15pt, "contributions of different films, interfaces, and the substrate to change with frequency and providing another route for ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 559.75pt, "multilayer parameter estimation. Ziade et al. used FDTR to measure the temperature-dependent interfacial thermal ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 575.38pt, "conductance of epitaxial GaN/SiC [87]. Song et al. combined FDTR and SSTR to characterize GaN-on-SiC wafers and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 590.98pt, "used the measured properties to validate device-level thermal models [88]. Delmas et al. used spatially resolved FDTR ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 606.58pt, "to map heat transport and stress across a compression-bonded GaN/diamond interface [89]. These studies show that ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 622.18pt, "changing frequency and spatial conditions can provide different sensitivity weights for multilayer and buried-interface ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 637.78pt, "problems, but this should not be interpreted as strict tomographic depth imaging. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 653.38pt, "For a multilayer stack such as GaN/Si, in which the cross-plane thermal-resistance distribution spans multiple ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 668.98pt, "characteristic scales (Fig. 8a1), however, one or a few fitted parameters are often insufficient to represent the actual ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 684.58pt, "heat-transport behavior. The near-surface GaN layer, AlGaN buffer layer, AlN transition layer, buried GaN/Si interface, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 700.18pt, "and Si substrate can all contribute to the thermoreflectance signal, and their relative contributions change with ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 715.78pt, "modulation frequency and heat-diffusion length. If all individual layer properties are fitted directly without first ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 731.38pt, "determining which parameter combinations are actually measurable, the optimization may converge mathematically to ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 747pt, "a result that is not physically unique. Identifying the experimentally measurable parameters is therefore itself a central ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 762.6pt, "problem in thermoreflectance inversion for complex multilayer systems. ")
]

