  #line-at(49.56pt, 99.5pt, "physical interpretations corresponding to cross-plane diffusion, lateral diffusion, and interfacial thermal relaxation, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 115.1pt, "rather than being merely mathematical regroupings of variables. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 130.7pt, "Figure 8 summarizes the study of a GaN/Si multilayer heterostructure by Chen et al. [55] using SPS and combined-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 146.3pt, "parameter analysis. The sample consisted of an approximately 87 nm Al transducer, 1.08 µm GaN, 460 nm AlGaN, 220 ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 161.9pt, "nm AlN, and a Si substrate (Fig. 8a1). A direct full multilayer thermal model contains 19 physical parameters, including ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 177.5pt, "layer thermal conductivities, volumetric heat capacities, thicknesses, interfacial thermal conductances, and spot ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 193.1pt, "parameters (Fig. 8a2). Nondimensionalization and combined-parameter analysis reorganize these into 13 combined ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 208.7pt, "parameters (Fig. 8a3). Because the AlN layer is thin and has relatively low thermal resistance, its contribution can be ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 224.3pt, "combined with those of adjacent interfaces into an equivalent thermal resistance, further reducing model complexity. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 239.9pt, "The value of combined-parameter analysis lies not only in reducing the dimensionality of the inverse problem, but more ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 255.53pt, "importantly in identifying which combinations are genuinely measurable in a complex multilayer system. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 271.13pt, "In this SPS example, different modulation frequencies produce clear changes in the relative sensitivities to the ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 286.73pt, "combined parameters. At 5 MHz (Fig. 8b1-b3), the thermal response is concentrated mainly in the Al transducer and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 302.33pt, "the near-surface portion of the GaN. At 750 kHz (Fig. 8c1-c3), the diffusion region extends farther into the GaN and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 317.93pt, "AlGaN buffer. At 150 kHz (Fig. 8d1-d3), substrate-related parameters carry greater weight. Thus, the \"layer selectivity\" ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 333.53pt, "in this case is more accurately understood as a frequency-dependent redistribution of sensitivity among layers and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 349.13pt, "combined parameters, rather than independent layer-by-layer imaging or strict depth separation. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 364.73pt, "In addition to the sensitivity changes provided by frequency, this SPS example uses the heating and cooling ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 380.33pt, "portions of the periodic waveform to increase discrimination among combined parameters. Near-surface heat capacity ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 395.93pt, "and interfacial thermal conductance, cross-plane film diffusion, in-plane diffusion, and substrate properties do not ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 411.55pt, "influence every part of the waveform in exactly the same way. Jointly fitting full-period responses at multiple ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 427.15pt, "frequencies allows candidate combined parameters with sufficiently high sensitivity and relatively low correlation to ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 442.75pt, "be selected, after which known layer thicknesses, spot size, and transducer areal heat capacity can be used to recover ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 458.35pt, "specific thermophysical properties. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 473.95pt, "Using this combined-parameter estimation strategy, Chen et al. [55] obtained several key thermophysical ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 489.67pt, "properties of the GaN/Si multilayer structure: Al/GaN interfacial thermal conductance ")
