#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "DengXian", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.85pt, 803.64pt, "39 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 68.28pt, "semiconductor process flows or finished-device inspection; transducerless measurements based on intrinsic optical ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 83.9pt, "responses are therefore particularly attractive for engineering applications, although variations in surface condition, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 99.5pt, "optical properties, and thermoreflectance coefficients can complicate quantitative calibration and large-area ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 115.1pt, "measurement consistency. Physics-informed machine learning, surrogate forward models, and precomputed model ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 130.7pt, "libraries may further accelerate inversion for complex structures, but physical constraints, uncertainty quantification, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 146.3pt, "and validation against independent or reference measurements remain necessary for reliable deployment. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 161.9pt, "Overall, device-oriented thermoreflectance is progressing from idealized samples toward operando device ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 177.5pt, "characterization, from predominantly thermal measurements toward coupled multiphysics interrogation, and from ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 193.1pt, "serial laboratory experiments toward higher-throughput engineering metrology. Future progress will depend not only ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 208.7pt, "on improved spatiotemporal resolution, but also on the ability to distinguish thermal signals from electrical, mechanical, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 224.3pt, "and optical contributions without substantially perturbing the operating state of the device. At the same time, increased ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 239.9pt, "acquisition speed, process-compatible measurement configurations, automated inversion, and rigorous uncertainty ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 255.53pt, "assessment will be required to translate laboratory techniques into robust engineering tools. Together, these ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 271.13pt, "developments could broaden the role of thermoreflectance from thermophysical-property measurement to spatially and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 286.73pt, "temporally resolved thermal diagnostics and metrology for power electronics, flexible devices, advanced packaging, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 302.33pt, "and semiconductor manufacturing. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 333.65pt, "5.4 Natural-Language-Driven Data Analysis and Intelligent Experimentation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.584pt, 356.93pt, "Beyond measurement resolution and inversion methodology, broader adoption of thermoreflectance is also ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 372.53pt, "constrained by the complexity of its analysis workflow and its dependence on specialized domain knowledge and user-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 388.13pt, "defined analysis choices. Methods such as TDTR, FDTR, and SPS typically require data organization and preprocessing, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 403.73pt, "definition of the multilayer structure, specification of known and unknown parameters, selection of fitting ranges and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 419.35pt, "experimental conditions, sensitivity analysis, parameter estimation, and uncertainty propagation. Even when mature ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 434.95pt, "computational codes or dedicated software packages are available, analysis of complex multilayer structures can remain ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 450.55pt, "strongly dependent on user experience, particularly in model construction, parameter selection, identifiability ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 466.15pt, "assessment, and interpretation of fitting results. This dependence complicates workflow standardization, reproducible ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 481.75pt, "high-throughput analysis, and broader interdisciplinary use. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 497.35pt, "AI agents based on large language models (LLMs) provide a potential route to workflow-level automation that is ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 512.95pt, "conceptually distinct from machine-learning models trained to predict thermophysical properties directly from ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 528.55pt, "experimental signals. Recent studies have begun to explore tool-augmented LLMs for scientific user facilities, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 544.15pt, "automated experimentation, and interaction with complex laboratory instrumentation [116–119]. For thermoreflectance, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 559.75pt, "a scientifically appropriate role for an LLM-based agent is to translate user intent into structured analysis tasks, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 575.38pt, "coordinate validated computational tools, and interpret their outputs, rather than to generate thermophysical-property ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 590.98pt, "values independently. Numerical calculations can remain within deterministic and validated heat-diffusion solvers, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 606.58pt, "fitting algorithms, sensitivity-analysis routines, and uncertainty-quantification modules, while the LLM provides ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 622.18pt, "natural-language interaction, workflow orchestration, and contextual reasoning across these components. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 637.78pt, "A layered architecture could therefore consist of a natural-language interaction layer, an AI-agent orchestration ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 653.38pt, "layer, and a validated physics-computation layer. Researchers could specify the sample structure, known parameters, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 668.98pt, "experimental data, and analysis objectives in natural language, after which the agent would translate these inputs into ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 684.58pt, "a machine-readable configuration, check required parameters and units, and sequentially invoke data preprocessing, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 700.18pt, "forward-model evaluation, sensitivity analysis, parameter fitting, and uncertainty-quantification modules. The outputs ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 715.78pt, "of each step—including model assumptions, parameter bounds, fitting settings, sensitivity results, uncertainties, and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 731.38pt, "software versions—could be recorded automatically to provide a traceable provenance chain. Such an architecture ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 747pt, "could shift thermoreflectance analysis from manual operation of specialized software toward reproducible, auditable ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 762.6pt, "workflows in which scientific intent is translated systematically into validated computational operations, while ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 778.2pt, "retaining the underlying physics model as the basis of quantitative inference. ")
]

// arXiv source page 40
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "DengXian", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.85pt, 803.64pt, "40 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.584pt, 68.28pt, "When such an agent is further connected to data-acquisition and instrument-control interfaces, it could form a ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 83.9pt, "closed loop with the adaptive experimental-design framework discussed in Section 5.1. Based on the measurements ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 99.5pt, "already acquired, the system could update parameter sensitivities and uncertainties and evaluate candidate experimental ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 115.1pt, "conditions according to expected information gain or another predefined design criterion. It could then propose—or, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 130.7pt, "where appropriate, execute after user confirmation—new modulation frequencies, delay-time windows, spot sizes, or ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 146.3pt, "spatial offsets that are expected to improve parameter identifiability or reduce uncertainty. This creates a potential ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 161.9pt, "progression from natural-language-assisted data analysis to adaptive experimentation, in which measurement selection ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 177.5pt, "and parameter inference are iteratively coupled rather than performed as separate stages. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 193.1pt, "Because thermophysical metrology requires quantitative reliability and reproducibility, however, LLM-based ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 208.7pt, "automation should not be treated as an unconstrained decision layer. Intelligent thermoreflectance systems should ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 224.3pt, "instead be built around validated domain-specific models and numerical codes, rigorous checks of parameter ranges, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 239.9pt, "dimensions, and units, machine-readable records of model assumptions and data transformations, complete provenance ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 255.53pt, "of computational and experimental operations, and explicit human confirmation for critical actions. Numerical outputs ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 271.13pt, "should remain traceable to the deterministic tools and experimental data that generated them, allowing calculations to ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 286.73pt, "be independently reproduced and audited rather than relying on the language model as the source of quantitative results. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 302.33pt, "The objective of intelligent thermoreflectance experimentation is therefore not automation for its own sake, but the ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 317.93pt, "development of a human-supervised, physics-grounded, and traceable analysis–experiment loop that combines natural-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 333.53pt, "language accessibility with the rigor required for quantitative thermophysical measurement. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 365.21pt, "6 ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 365.21pt, "Summary ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.584pt, 388.13pt, "This review has systematically examined thermoreflectance-based micro- and nanoscale thermophysical-property ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 403.73pt, "measurement, covering the physical foundations, experimental configurations, signal-acquisition strategies, and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 419.35pt, "application regimes of representative techniques including TTR, TDTR, FDTR, SSTR, SDTR, and SPS. Although these ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 434.95pt, "methods differ substantially in experimental implementation, they can be understood within a common framework of ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 450.55pt, "photothermal excitation, heat transport, thermoreflectance detection, and model-based parameter inference. Their ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 466.15pt, "principal distinction lies in the measurement coordinate and observable through which the thermal response is ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 481.75pt, "interrogated: TTR records single-pulse transient decay; TDTR resolves ultrafast thermal evolution through pump–probe ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 497.35pt, "delay; FDTR measures frequency-dependent amplitude and phase; SSTR probes the quasi-steady temperature response; ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 512.95pt, "SDTR and beam-offset approaches introduce lateral spatial information; and SPS captures the full temperature ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 528.55pt, "waveform under periodic square-wave excitation. These techniques should therefore be viewed not as competing ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 544.15pt, "variants of a single measurement, but as complementary experimental projections of the same underlying heat-transport ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 559.75pt, "problem, providing different sensitivity signatures across characteristic length and time scales. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 575.38pt, "In practical applications, method selection should account jointly for sample geometry, target thermophysical ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 590.98pt, "properties, available prior information, instrument bandwidth, and the identifiability of the desired parameter set under ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 606.58pt, "the accessible experimental conditions. TDTR and FDTR are widely applied to cross-plane film thermal conductivity ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 622.18pt, "and interfacial thermal conductance, whereas SDTR and beam-offset configurations can introduce enhanced spatial ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 637.78pt, "sensitivity to in-plane transport and thermal anisotropy. For low-thermal-conductivity materials or strongly coupled ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 653.38pt, "multilayer systems, low-frequency FDTR, multi-condition TDTR, SPS, extended transient measurements, or joint ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 668.98pt, "analysis of complementary measurement configurations can be employed according to the relevant heat-diffusion scales ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 684.58pt, "and required parameter sensitivities. Regardless of technique, strong sensitivity to an individual parameter does not by ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 700.18pt, "itself guarantee that the parameter can be uniquely determined when other unknowns produce correlated responses. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 715.78pt, "Measurement credibility therefore depends on an appropriate forward model, accurate structural and optical inputs, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 731.38pt, "sufficiently distinct parameter sensitivities, and rigorous uncertainty assessment. No single technique or experimental ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 747pt, "condition can consequently be regarded as universally optimal for complex multiparameter characterization. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 762.6pt, "Future development of thermoreflectance can be considered along four interconnected directions. First, advances ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 778.2pt, "in temporal and spatial resolution will extend measurements toward shorter timescales and smaller transport dimensions, ")
]

// arXiv source page 41
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "DengXian", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.85pt, 803.64pt, "41 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 68.28pt, "enabling further investigation of ultrafast thermal relaxation, quasiballistic phonon transport, nonequilibrium interfaces, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 83.9pt, "and localized heat transfer in micro- and nanostructures. Such gains in resolution must be accompanied by ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 99.5pt, "corresponding advances in model fidelity as experiments approach the boundaries of conventional Fourier heat ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 115.1pt, "diffusion. Second, integration with electrical excitation, mechanical loading, near-field optical techniques, and in situ ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 130.7pt, "or operando device measurements will expand thermoreflectance from isolated thermal characterization toward ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 146.3pt, "multiphysics measurements under realistic operating conditions. Third, data analysis is expected to progress from ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 161.9pt, "single-optimum fitting toward uncertainty-aware inference that combines sensitivity and identifiability analysis, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 177.5pt, "probabilistic parameter estimation, model-credibility assessment, and physics-based constraints. Fourth, advances in ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 193.1pt, "scientific AI may enable natural-language interfaces and agent-based workflow orchestration, in which experimental ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 208.7pt, "intent is translated into structured analysis and tool execution while quantitative inference remains grounded in ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 224.3pt, "validated physical models and traceable numerical calculations. Coupling these capabilities with uncertainty-aware ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 239.9pt, "experimental design could further establish closed loops among measurement, inference, and condition selection, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 255.53pt, "enabling more efficient and adaptive acquisition of informative data. ")
  #line-at(70.584pt, 271.13pt, "Overall, thermoreflectance has developed into a versatile platform for micro- and nanoscale thermophysical ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 286.73pt, "characterization. Its strength lies not only in noncontact optical interrogation, high temporal resolution, and localized ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 302.33pt, "measurement capability, but also in the ability to manipulate heat-flow geometry and parameter sensitivity through ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 317.93pt, "experimental variables such as modulation frequency, pump–probe delay, spot size, and spatial position or offset. The ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 333.53pt, "central opportunity for future thermoreflectance is therefore not simply to extend measurement ranges or increase data-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 349.13pt, "acquisition speed, but to integrate experimental design, multiscale physical modeling, parameter identifiability, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 364.73pt, "uncertainty quantification, and reproducible workflow control. As these elements become increasingly integrated, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 380.33pt, "thermoreflectance can evolve from a collection of specialized laboratory techniques toward a more unified, quantitative, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 395.93pt, "traceable, and adaptive thermal-metrology framework, supporting increasingly complex applications in functional thin ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 411.55pt, "films, heterogeneous interfaces, power electronics, advanced packaging, and semiconductor-process monitoring. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
